{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>\"The Book of the Wars of YHWH\"</b> — And the way of the peshat is that in those generations there were wise men who would write a book of the great wars, as is the case in every generation. The authors of such books were called מושלים (makers of parables), because parables and figures of speech were drawn from them, and the marvelous victories in their eyes — they attributed those wars to YHWH, for truly they are His. Now, the might of Sihon over Moav was wondrous in their eyes, and they recorded it in a book and composed figures of speech concerning it: \"את והב בסופה\" and so on, and they drew a parable about it: \"Come to Heshbon\" and so on (Numbers 21:27). Now, \"והב\" is the name of one of the cities that belonged to Moav, and \"אשד הנחלים\" is the slope of the wadi, for the wadi-waters flow and descend from the slopes of the Pisgah (Deuteronomy 3:17), and likewise \"the hill-country and the Negev and the Lowland and the slopes\" (Joshua 10:40). \"בסופה\" is from the expression \"בסופה ובשערה\" (Nahum 1:3). And so, when Sihon captured the cities of Moav, the מושלים wrote in the book that they called \"The Wars of YHWH\": \"את והב בסופה,\" or perhaps they wrote: YHWH fought against Vahev at Suphah and against the wadis of the Arnon — the outpouring of the wadis that extended toward the settlement of Ar, and the slope leaned against the border of Moav — all of it YHWH destroyed in stormwind and tempest, for Sihon came upon them suddenly; the hoofs of his horses were reckoned like a besieger and his wheels like the stormwind. And likewise they said: \"For a fire went out from Heshbon, a flame from the city of Sihon\" and so on (Numbers 21:28). Now, the verse brings proof from the Book of the Wars that the Arnon is the border of Moav and is forbidden to Israel, while the wadis and all the slopes up to the Arnon are permitted to them, because Sihon took from the king of Moav all his land up to the Arnon, the Arnon itself not included, and the Arnon remained to Moav and serves as its border, as it is written: \"And to the Reubenite and the Gadite I gave from Gilead as far as the wadi of Arnon, the middle of the wadi and the border\" (Deuteronomy 3:16). And so Jephthah said: \"And they encamped beyond the Arnon and did not enter the border of Moav, for the Arnon is the border of Moav\" (Judges 11:18)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:33.512403145Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}